## Design system contract (Design handoff + EDS)

This section encodes where design-system assets live, what to reuse, and what never to hardcode. RAD's source of truth is the canonical design handoff (`src/design-handoff/`) + EDS. The configured design tool, via its adapter, reads the codebase and produces a handoff matching `artifacts/docs/handoff-contract.md`.

| Design-system rule | RAD equivalent |
| --- | --- |
| Read structured design before coding | **Read** the handoff TSX in `src/design-handoff/` (during Foundation, before Step 5 cleanup) or `artifacts/docs/design-reference/web/` (after Foundation, for mobile translation per Step 4b), **plus** `artifacts/docs/screen-specs-*-v1.md` and **`artifacts/docs/design-system-spec.md`** after Foundation catalogs the handoff |
| Token / component discovery | **`design-system-spec.md`** (inventory + gaps); live primitives in **`src/components/ui/`**; tokens in **`src/app.css`** (from the handoff's `theme.css`) |
| Do not bolt on duplicate libraries | **IMPORTANT:** the adapter's `components/ui` **is** the library — same as elsewhere in this file |
| Asset discipline | Use images/icons **from the handoff bundle**; self-host fonts per `frontend-design.mdc`; do **not** add icon packages to replicate glyphs the adapter already ships |

**Before changing layout, colors, or adding a "new" UI primitive:** Check `design-system-spec.md` and existing `src/components/ui/` — extend or compose; do not introduce a parallel component set.

When **native** mode is active, brand colors/types that land in **`shared/colors.ts`** and `mobile/global.css` must **stay aligned** with EDS §5 and web tokens (see `mobile-developer.md` Foundation).

